* GnuCap simulation — gpio_button_timing
* LED branch: GP17 (3.3V) -> R_limit(220Ω) -> D_led(LED) -> GND
* Button pull-down: 3V3 -> R_pull(10kΩ) -> GP16 (active-high, pull-down)

* --- LED drive branch ---
V_gp17 1 0 DC 3.3
R_limit 1 2 220
D_led 2 0 LED

.model LED D Is=1e-14 Rs=5

* --- Button pull-down (button closed = GP16 pulled HIGH via 3V3) ---
V_3v3 4 0 DC 3.3
R_pull 4 3 10000

* Sweep GP17 output 0 → 3.3V to verify LED current stays safe (<20mA)
.dc V_gp17 0 3.3 0.05

* v(2) = LED anode; i(D_led) = LED current; v(3) = GP16 node (button-pressed ~3.3V)
.print dc v(2) i(D_led) v(3)

.end
